TEXT 64 32 Left 2 ;RC high-pass filter
TEXT 64 656 Left 2 !.ac dec 200 10 1Meg
TEXT 64 704 Left 2 ;R1 = 1k, C1 = 100n: cutoff about 1.59 kHz.
TEXT 64 768 Left 2 ;1. Click Run: the running-person button at the top left.
TEXT 64 808 Left 2 ;2. On the schematic, click the wire labeled VOUT (not the component).
TEXT 64 848 Left 2 ;3. Read the response: frequency on X, gain in dB on Y.
TEXT 64 888 Left 2 ;If the plot is empty, select the schematic window and click the labeled wire again.
TEXT 64 968 Left 2 ;EXPERIMENTS AND COMMON QUESTIONS
TEXT 64 1008 Left 2 ;Right-click a component to edit its value. Predict first, change one value, then Run.
TEXT 64 1048 Left 2 ;TRY: Double C1. The high-pass cutoff moves lower.
TEXT 64 1088 Left 2 ;WHY: At low frequency C1 has large impedance; at high frequency it passes signal.
TEXT 64 1128 Left 2 ;Probe VIN and VOUT; the passband tends to 0 dB with this ideal source.
